# =============================================================================
# CRITICAL — Atlas evaluation integrity boundary
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# data/ground_truth.json is the sealed answer key. The agent must NEVER see it.
# Only the eval harness (eval/) may read it. Keeping it out of git ensures it
# cannot be accidentally surfaced through repo search, IDE indexing, or a stray
# import. Do not remove this line. See docs/atlas-prd.md §7 and CLAUDE.md.
#
# scripts/generate_data.py is the equivalent of a second answer key. It contains
# the explicit pattern-placement logic — HIDDEN_CHURN_IDS, EXPANSION_IDS, the
# deterministic seed (SEED = 20260519), per-pattern weekly modifiers, and the
# random shuffle that decides which accounts carry which patterns. Anyone who
# reads it (or re-runs it) can reconstruct the answer key, so it must not be
# tracked in git. The structural validator scripts/validate_data.py is safe to
# read and IS committed. Do not remove these lines. See CLAUDE.md.
# =============================================================================
data/ground_truth.json
scripts/generate_data.py

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/
env/

